  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% benchmark and per-model results for regulators and customers, with public release limited to aggregated data, but contains no obligation to stop sales of an above-limit model. S5 keeps an objective 8-per-100,000 recall trigger with no bounded corrective alternative, which exposes the Ember 8 (9.9) to mandatory recall. S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window favouring Northwind, and S1 limits reporting of minor overheating events, which weakens reporting for both companies."
 },
